# CASM progress-indication Increment 8 trusted reference: casmpgr6
#
# Independently hand-derived, NOT produced by CASM. casmpgr6.seq has no
# .ORG (relocatable mode, default origin $3400) and a forward label
# reference, so the R6 footer carries one real relocation entry -- the
# case that exercises the WRITE line and the emitFlush + relocation-table
# + 6-byte-footer byte accounting the progress DONE summary reports.
#
# Source (no .ORG):
#   - START:  (label)
#   -   NOP  x 40
#   -   JMP TARGET
#   - TARGET: (label)
#   -   NOP
#
# START = $3400. 40 NOP occupy $3400..$3427. JMP (opcode $4C, 3 bytes) is
# at $3428..$342A; TARGET resolves to $342B, so JMP encodes "4C 2B 34".
# JMP's ValHi byte ($34) is at program offset $342A-$3400 = $2A -- the
# sole relocation entry.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 34        PRG load-address header ($3400, little-endian)
#   EA x 40      NOP (implied), $3400..$3427
#   4C 2B 34     JMP $342B    (forward reference resolved to TARGET)
#   EA           NOP          (at $342B, defines TARGET)
#   2A 00        R6 table: one entry, offset $2A (JMP's ValHi byte)
#   00 34        R6 footer: base address ($3400, little-endian)
#   01 00        R6 footer: relocation entry count (1)
#   52 36        R6 footer: ASCII magic "R6"
#
# bytes: 54
